  "header": "The cyber model is not in ChatGPT. The bank connection is, if you pay.",
  "friendlyHeader": "The new security model is not in ChatGPT. Claude can look at your bank, if you turn it on.",
  "summary": "On 5 November, OpenAI released GPT-6 Cyber for a short list of approved security teams, not for a normal ChatGPT account. The same day, Anthropic started a US beta that lets paid Claude users connect a bank account, read-only. A two-person lab also published a 2-billion-parameter image model and said the training run cost about $21,000. The useful split is still access: what you can open today, and what stays behind an application.",
  "friendlySummary": "On 5 November, OpenAI released a cybersecurity model for approved security teams. It is not in a normal ChatGPT account. The same day, Anthropic started a test for paid Claude users in the United States. You can connect a bank account. Claude can read the transactions. It cannot move the money. A two-person lab also published an image model and said the training cost about $21,000. The useful question is what you can open today, and what stays on a list.",
